One-page cheat sheet linking to the full manuals. Keep this file short —
use the linked manuals for details.

## Key quick commands (updated for Mycelium manager)

- Create a PC and generate graphs:

```bash
python3 create_pc.py --name Bob --run-update --make-graphs
```

- Update a single Character Sheet:

```bash
python3 update_char.py --pc Bob
```

- Regenerate root + per-PC graphs (union of `pcs_input.md` and existing HTMLs):

```bash
python3 Wikigraphs.py --pc --all -v
```

- Mycelium: quick bulk file operations

Mycelium's new lightweight file manager is `Mycelium/Wiki_File_System_Manager.py`.
It supports bulk find/replace, collectionfile maintenance, and tagging/graph features.

Examples (run from repo root):

- Preview inferred tags for all markdown files (no writes):

```bash
python3 Mycelium/Wiki_File_System_Manager.py --paths Mycelium --include "**/*.md" --infer-tags
```

- Add tags `#forest` and `#npc` to all scanned files (dry-run, then write with backup):

```bash
python3 Mycelium/Wiki_File_System_Manager.py --paths Mycelium --include "**/*.md" --add-tags forest npc --dry-run
python3 Mycelium/Wiki_File_System_Manager.py --paths Mycelium --include "**/*.md" --add-tags forest npc --backup .bak
```

- Remove a tag from files:

```bash
python3 Mycelium/Wiki_File_System_Manager.py --paths Mycelium --include "**/*.md" --remove-tags oldtag --backup .bak
```

- Export a JSON graph (nodes/edges) describing wikilinks and parent edges:

```bash
python3 Mycelium/Wiki_File_System_Manager.py --paths Mycelium --include "**/*.md" --export-graph Mycelium/graphs/mygraph.json
```

- Write a `root_mushroomlist_settings` block into each file (useful for mushroom creation):

```bash
python3 Mycelium/Wiki_File_System_Manager.py --paths Mycelium --include "**/*.md" --write-root-mushrooms RootA RootB --backup .bak
```

Useful flags (summary):

- `--paths <paths...>` — root paths to scan (defaults to `.`).
- `--include <glob...>` / `--exclude-dir <name...>` — control files scanned.
- `--ext .md .txt` — restrict by file extensions.
- `--dry-run` — preview changes without writing.
- `--backup .bak` — create backups when writing.
- `--add-tags` / `--remove-tags` — bulk tag operations (no leading `#`).
- `--infer-tags` — print candidate tags inferred from folder names, links, filename.
- `--export-graph <out.json>` — write nodes/edges JSON of the vault subset.
- `--write-root-mushrooms` — write a JSON list block between `<!-- BEGIN-ROOT-MUSHROOMS -->` and `<!-- END-ROOT-MUSHROOMS -->`.
- `--recreate-collectionfiles` / `--collectionfile <path>` — the collectionfile helpers remain available.

## Where to look

- Graphs: `graphs/<Name>_wikigraph_sunburst.html` and `graphs/<Name>_wikigraph_treemap.html`.
- Mycelium files: `Mycelium/` folder contains the manager, helper scripts, and mushroom outputs.

